= The Lighthouse Keeper

The storm had been building since noon, and by the time Mara reached the
harbour the sky over the water had gone the colour of slate. She stood at the
end of the pier with her collar turned up, watching the beam of the lighthouse
sweep across the waves.

"You'll catch your death out here," said a voice behind her.

She didn't turn around. She had known Tomas would come; he always did, when
the weather was bad and the boats were late. _Especially_ when the boats were
late.

#scene-break()

The keeper's cottage smelled of tar and woodsmoke. Tomas set two mugs on the
table and sat down across from her, and for a long while neither of them said
anything at all.
